{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires","id":1510211,"title":"Have you created your own origins for the vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-30T10:38:16-07:00","id":1510211,"title":"Have you created your own origins for the vampires?","content":"While I personally love notion of Set being the father of the undead and selecting 12 people to fight his enemies. I\u2019m curious if you came up with your backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T11:42:13-07:00","id":1510230,"title":"","content":"I used the different creation myths of the vampires - but not created my own myth<br /> I have gathered several and used them, thoguh I will share it with you - in the games where I used them, it made the story exciting, gave it a bit more depth - especially to the stories where we played throgh the ages, and one vampire race tried to destroy the other and always fun to throw a curve ball to some noddist-wannabee!<br /> Anyhow, my list:<br /> <br /> <b>Caine/Khayyin</b> [VtM]<br /> Your generic vampire progenitor, we all know his stroy, tho its fun to tweak it a little, since his story tells, God really favored Abel's sacrifice over Caine's. So Caine &quot;sacrificing&quot; Abel on an altar, his brother being the &quot;finest&quot; offering he could give. As punishment, Cain's &quot;Father&quot; cursed him with a mark, and cast him out to wander in darkness in the Land of Nod. &quot;Father&quot; could be interpeted as God/Jehovah (or one of the gods around with Gardens aka. Revelations of the Dark Mother), and Lilith, Adam's original whife tho' hesitant how the Awekening Ceremony will react to the Mark and the Sevenfold Curse, preformed it anyhow. If you are in to Mage things, the vampiric curses are severe Paradox backslashes, or if you love traditional route, Michael, when denied, cursed Caine and his childer to fear his living flame. Raphael cursed Caine and his childer to fear the dawn, as the sun's rays would burn like fire. Uriel then cursed Caine and his childer to cling to Darkness, drink only blood, eat only ashes, and be frozen at the point of death, cursed so all they touch would crumble into nothing. A fourth angel, Gabriel, then appeared to offer the way of Golconda, the only way to &quot;light&quot;, by the mercy of God. Wich really makes the descendats of Caine simpathetic, fellow Cursed to any Fallen crossover. Interestingly enough, Caine's myth never really says Caine ever died... just recived a tons of curses and passed those down to freshly killed corpses rised by his blood.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bloody Man</b> [Silver Records]<br /> The Bloody Man is the first vampire on Earth according to Garou mythology. Weaver was impatient for mankind to turn towards her. Unable to approach them openly, for the Garou guarded their families ferociously, she stole a man and wove her webs around him. The man's internal spark of the Wyld was snuffed and his spirit left his body. However, through the Weaver's work, he was unable to die and begged her to save him from the fate of decomposition - the Weaver obliged and soon found herself enthralled in her newest servant. The Man, now immortal, became greedy and learned from the Weaver how to manipulate the strands of the Pattern Web for his own use. This intrusion angered the - still uncorrupted - Wyrm, who swallowed the Man to return him to the cycle of being. But the Man was still immortal and within the Wyrm's belly, he began to feed on the blood of the Great Devourer. The Wyrm, howling in pain, spat out the blood-soaked Man, whom all of creation abhorred. Helios then cast his angry gaze upon him, and the Bloody Man was forced to flee beneath the earth. Gaia herself cursed him to hunger forever for blood, to enter age-lasting sleep without dreams and to be unable to conceive and only able to corrupt. Helios warned the Bloody Man that if he or his progeny would ever show his face to him again, he would burn them to cinders. The Bloody Man entered a long-lasting sleep beneath the earth and awakened several centuries later. In the meantime, the Wyrm was weakened by the internal wounds the Bloody Man had inflicted upon it, later allowing the Weaver to trap it in its webs.<br /> The Bloody Man is a very ancient... thing. And by corruption and blood and dark powers, his vampiric line is more like the cross of a Risen and a Fomor. They are a bit the neanderthals of the vampires. Predators with darkness in them with the need of Order, thanks to their ancestor's weaver-conection. Or like how the Nictuku hunts their &quot;lesser&quot; Nosferatu brothers, the line of the Bloody Man hunts the other vampires. Tossing in to the mix the Predator of the Predators is always funny...<br /> <br /> <b>Cagn</b> [Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom]<br /> The Laibon speak of Cagn, who courted the daughter of the sun and married her after impressing her how clever and self-sustaining surviver he was thanks to a fetish that he recived from his mother that had the power to turn anything to anything, like a blade of grass in to a spear. He tried to conquer the Land of the Dead and fought with the Lion of Death. Who killed him and evoured him leaving only some bones behind. His brother Nakati who posessed a similar fetish stole the coprse of his brother from the Lion of Death and using their two fetish brought him back to life. But the village of the Sun, the Sun itself and Cagn's whife, the daughter of the sun, Dasse celebrated Nakati as a hero from bringing back their beloved Cagn to them. Wich made Cagn very morose. The Lion of Death arrived and demanded the meat that was stolen from him, Cagn. Who decided to hide, instead of fighting and after his brother complained, killed him and tossed him to the Lion. After the Lion of Death realised he was decived, his anger was tremendous, cursed Cagn and the nine of his followers who helped him to decive the Lion and were like sons to him, to never again be able to enter the beautifull Land of the Dead, a tongue of fire forever burn in their mouth and the hunger of the All-Devourer forever gnaw at their belly. Cagn and his nine followers lamented and walied and the daughter of the Sun seeing her husband weeping like a child hid her face in shame and dissapeared from the word. The samed and angered Sun added his curse to the Lion of Death's curse, banishing Cagn from his light and everyone who is able to see up to the Sun be the enemy of Cagn and his people, then departed too to the havens following his daughter. Cagn and his nine followers dissapeard in to the eternal night of Africa, later those nine became the progenitors of the Nine &quot;native&quot; Laibon legacies.<br /> A funny little twist, to make the Vampires of Africa and the Vampires of the &quot;white people&quot; so different, they are completly different vampiric race.<br /> <br /> <b>Sutekh/Set</b> [Clanbook Settite]<br /> The sun-god Ra grew old and decided to retire. He chose his great-grandson Osiris as his heir and successor. But that did not sit well with Osiris\u2019 brother, Set, for he was the mightiest warrior among the gods who guarded the sun-barque of Ra every night as it passed under the Earth from the gates of sunset to the gates of dawn, battling Apophis, the Great Serpent of Darkness. The succession of Ra brought great strife among his descendents. Set\u2019s jealousy and wounded pride drove him to murder his brother through trickery. He hacked his brother\u2019s body to bits and scattered them about Egypt. Patiently, Isis gathered the fragments, reassembled the body of Osiris and used her magic to conceive a child by her dead husband. When their child Horus grew to manhood, he challenged Set for the kingship of the gods. Some legends speak of mighty battles between gods and armies. Other tales describe their strife as a farcical court case, full of low tricks and silly contests. One way or another, Horus prevailed. Horus lost an eye in their strife; in revenge, he castrated Set. Osiris, meanwhile, became King of the Dead just as his son became King of the Living; and the Pharaonic dynasties henceforth claimed to rule by descent from Horus the Avenger. As compensation, Ra gave Set two foreign goddesses as concubines and made him god of storms. In another version of this tale Ra is depicted as a malevolent tyrant. It is said the \u201cFirst City\u201d, was called Annu, and it was the city of Ra. The story goes much like the version mentioned above, but it has a radically different ending. According to this version, after the triumph of Horus, Ra turned on his defender and cursed Set to live in darkness forever. Then the gods thrust Set into Duat, the dark Underworld of the dead, and the river of death whose waters come from the Primeval Ocean itself, where Set fought the great serpent Apophis once more. He slew the Worm of Darkness and ate its heart. With Apep\u2019s death Set took on Apep\u2019s dark wisdom and learned secrets hidden from the beginning of the world. When Ra had created the world, he gave it life through his own semen, creating gods and the souls of human beings alike. Souls differed in size but not in kind. Jealous Ra lied to all his children. He told them that he was mightiest of all things, creator of the universe, when he merely shaped a tiny portion of the Primeval Waters. Now, however, Set knew the truth: all souls could grow as mighty as their tyrant father and become creators themselves. Set swore to overthrow Ra \u2013 not to get revenge, but to liberate the souls of humanity that Ra held in bondage. It so happens that the Primeval Waters carry life as well as death, and every year, the gates of the world open to let the Primeval Waters bring new life through the yearly inundation of the Nile. Set disguised himself as a water-serpent and slipped through the gates with the rushing waters. Despite the power gained from Apep, Set still had to hide from the sun; he could not break the curse of Ra. Nor did he truly live, for he had tasted the waters of death. As he walked the night, however, he recruited twelve talented disciples. He taught them the truth, and together they swore an oath to bring down Ra and the other false gods and become gods themselves. Set mingled his blood with that of his Disciples and when they drank of it, he gave up the greater share of his power, granting all thirteen almost equal might (although, as a true god, he remained the most powerful). But when Ra learned from the Moon that Set had defeated Apophis and escaped the Underworld, he extended his curse to the twelve human disciples with whom Set had shared blood, decreeing that all who joined Set\u2019s rebellion against the gods would share his banishment from the Sun and his castration, and that having sealed their pact in blood the thirteen would feed on blood alone. Set's disciples begged for mercy, claiming Set had misled them, thus betraying Set and his teachings. Their betrayal outraged Set (he always did have a short temper), and he swore that if they would not help him fight the gods, after all he had given them, he would destroy them as well, though it take him a million years<br /> Do I really need to elaborate the potential of this?^^<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Canarl</b> [Wolves of the Sea]<br /> Canarl was the first vampire according to einherjar myth called &quot;The Blood Saga&quot;.<br /> Odin One-Eye, lord of the slain and necromancer, came to Midgard with his valkyries to find warriors of valor. Among the dead they would pick and choose, taking up the most skilled and courageous to stay in Valhalla, where they would feast and fight until Ragnarok came to claim the gods and shake the world. With spear and runes Odin walked through the fields of the dying, seeking the warrior who would slay the jotunn and forge the destiny of the new world after Midgards's end. On the fields of one terrible battle Odin found a warrior of great strength and tenacity. Cast out by his family for his rage, this berserk drew about him a loyal band of housecarls who shared his fortunes and fought with him in all things. But wounded in war, laid low by evil spaework and telling blows, they were scattered dead across the plains of battle, where blood stained the earth like red iron. Only the lone berserk still lived, his outlaw body refusing to heed the call of Heimdall's horn. For vitality and skill Odin marked the dying warrior; coming low upon the man, he whispered to the man's dying spirit, asking his name so he could adress him in Valhalla. &quot;Canarl, I am named&quot; gasped the outlaw, &quot;Called the bastard, for my family disowned me. I have fought many fields of battle ever since, but by the rune-mark on my forehead I may never die.&quot; Odin looked upon the man's head and saw there the mark and knew his words where true. Then, with seeing from his one eye did Odin read the threads of fate, and cast the lot of Canarl. &quot;As your valor stands against death, so shall you stand against the ravages of time. Your skill is mighty but by my hand it shall be mightier. your blood spilled on this field makes the ground red; I shall turn my blood to you, and through it you will know my strength. Be strong the thews of your legs! Be mighty the grip of your spear! By the rune-mark on your forehead you shall never be touched by age: by the arts of war shall you rule!&quot; As Odin spoke he brought his spear, Gungnir, down to face Canarl, and from its tip did run the bright red blood of the god. Three drops fell upon the lips of Canarl, and he was struck with battle-frenzy; his body twisted and his lungs choked, and he died yet lived! With the mighty pronouncements of fate and the power of his blood, Odin gave Canarl eternity, but fate demanded satiation. Odin's eye stared again into the ways of the future and he intoned the demands of the Norns. &quot;With this bond in secret made you must ever hide from discovery, and so shall you shun the light of the sun and fire. No meat contains the potence to sustain you, no mead can intoxicate you; only the blood of men can bring warmth to your breast. From the lifeblood of the strong is your puissance multiplied. Blood you have spilled, and more blood still shall you spill; and only by coming closer to my blood shall your house know greatness.&quot; At length, Odin spoke a final time, this time slowly and with deliberation, saying, &quot;But if you scorn the ways of war, if you take up the mantle of the Vanir, then you shall stand beside them in the final nights; put aside spear and axe and you will know no peace from brethren but those whom you will find in Vanaheim. In the words of the Vanir you will survive with the gentle while the warriors know glory and death at Ragnarok.&quot; Odin drew back from Canarl, drew up his spear and called for his ravens. Canarl rose from the ground, and to his left he placed his wounds on the mouth of Ivar, his thegn (Military leader, akin to a warrior-king or colonel), who then rose; and to his right he placed his wounds upon the mouth of Odindisa, his wife, who then rose; and before him he placed his wounds upon the mouth of Eyjolf, his skald (Bard, poet), who then rose. And they gathered to them the sacraments of the dead, and built there a city raised to Odin. So say the einherjar of the Norse.<br /> The people of Canarl, the einherjar are a lovely addition to the game anyhow, and with their fixation to prepare the Ragnarok and be Odin's chosen warriors who will be able to shape the future are the treasuretrove of Vampire race-wars<br /> <br /> <b>Zapathasura</b> [Clanbook Ravnos]<br /> The birth of the Ravnos, and perhaps all vampires, is recorded in an epic poem called the Karavalanisha Vrana, translated as Wounds of the Night's Sword. The god's appointed protectors of humanity, the siddhittizaya, had been corrupted by the demons they were charged to fight and had taken to devouring the flesh, blood, and souls of mortals. Outraged, the gods cursed them, naming them asuratizayya or &quot;countless demons&quot; and declaring that from now on they would only find sustenance in devouring flesh and blood. This only encouraged the asuratizayya, however, who embraced their sins and gorged on humanity. Dismayed by this turn of events, the gods agreed to create a foe that would make the asuratizayya know true terror and curtail their gluttony. To that end, the gods took the soul of the man most grievously wronged by the asuratizayya and gave him new life, making him a monster so that he and his descendants might hunt the asuratizayya. Though many of the gods bestowed him with great gifts to further his cause, not all of them agreed to creating another dark force in the world. Three placed curses upon the man so that he should fear falling into temptation as the siddhittizaya had, and so the man would forever be threatened by the touch of fire and sunlight, and would also know an eternity of physical and spiritual hunger just as the creatures he hunted. Named Zapathasura, or &quot;accursed demon&quot;, he was then sent out to drive the infernal hordes from the world.<br /> Ahh the eternal bridge between the Kindred of the East line and the &quot;western&quot; world. Of yourse you have to love these things. I can't blame you if not, its an aquired taste^^<br /> <br /> <b>Ramanga</b> [Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition]<br /> The story of the Ramanga began on an island off Africa's south-east coast. On this island lived a woman called Ramanga and her brother, Rafazi. In this time, the ancestors of the Vazimba people, to which Ramanga belonged, were patriarchal. While Ramanga was the oldest child of the king and exceedingly smart as well as ambitious, the younger Rafazi was marked as heir. Unwilling and unable to accept a secondary role, Ramanga made sacrifices to the spirits of her people to bribe them into raising her above Rafazi. When that did not work, she began sacrificing to increasingly darker spirits until one of them finally answered her call. The spirit offered to lift Ramanga up if she would only sacrifice the sun inside her as payment. Heart already burdened by the unfairness of her situation and envy towards her brother, Ramanga willingly agreed. During the course of seven nights, the dark spirit initiated Ramanga in its heritage of shadows and illusion, showing her that real power lay not in giving orders, but in making them. Outward power might lie with the king, but real power lay with his advisors, the spirit said. Taking these lessons to heart, Ramanga returned to her people to ostensibly support her brother, even while she deftly manipulated him to do only her bidding. Cementing her control over Rafazi and his children with the power inherent to her sunless blood, Ramanga directed the future of the kingdom from that night onward. Her influence was even so great, that the Vazimba came to favor queens over kings, though it is not known if Ramanga deliberately manipulated this development, or if her mere presence instilled a sense of female rulership in the land.<br /> Loaded gun, I know, but god, this one is funy to have around, trust me!<br /> <br /> <b>Bonsam</b> [Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition]<br /> The first of the Bonsam claims to have never actually been Embraced, having been brought to unlife by a darkness from before creation, nor has he Embraced any childer; if this claim is in fact true, the Bonsam may have originated as an artificial bloodline, although other Bonsam can and do Embrace normally. After the Dark Ages, the Great Bonsam elder refused to enrich its lineage with gifts of blood and, in its madness, tried to devour its own line. Those who escaped decided to thicken their blood with transfusions from other lineages. In South Africa, they utilized blood from a Tzimisce explorer, founding the Nagloper lineage. Few of the original Bonsam remain, and vampires who adopt the name are either making a statement against the superstition and doom that follows the line, or are believed to be fools begging for their predecessor's curse. Lineages descended from the Bonsam often Embrace wily, hardy survivors.<br /> Okay, this vampire-race is a funny one in my book, really, it is just fun to have around an ultimate great monster who was made what it is by something premodial. A bit like the Bloody Man, they are excelent vampires other vampires could fear<br /> <br /> <b>The Twins</b><br /> According to Gangrel myth, thousands of years ago there was a god who had many children and his children fought as children are expected to do. Ennoia and Churka, the youngest and a pair of twins, chose to leave their quarrelsome siblings and travel east to the lands of their mother. Unable to escape their quarrelsome nature and without a father to control them, the twins came to blows. Evenly and perfectly matched, they could not face each other directly with a definite victor. And so the twins began to recruit armies \u2013 Ennoia recruited an army of the bravest warriors, and Churka, the most cunning. They battled at night, so that the other gods would not learn of their feud. These two armies fought for centuries but at some point, when it was believed Ennoia's army would finally have victory, she was betrayed by her two best warriors. Without two of her generals, however, the battle tilted in the favor of Churka's army. Saddened by this betrayal, Ennoia left her childer and disappeared. Soon, without the support of their progenitor, and battling Churka's get \u2013 who were aided by the demonic Giants of the East (the Kuei-jin) that served him \u2013 Ennoia's army was eventually defeated and pushed out of their lands in the east. From that night on they called themselves the Gangrel, and traveled West, meeting the Cainites. Even today, some Gangrel believe that when Churka and his army are destroyed and the betrayers punished, Ennoia would finally come back to her children.<br /> Before V5 Proean and the Gangrel Clan was something... strange, I always felt, they simply don't belong in to the Cainite society. Like the Ravnos or the Followers of Set. Why? Hey,becasue they are not even Cainites! Fun? Yes please!<br /> <br /> <b>Ixion</b><br /> In the Dark Ages and prior that many vampire belived they are the descendants of Ixion.<br /> Ixion married Dia, a daughter of Deioneus (or Eioneus), and promised his father-in-law a valuable present. However, he did not pay the bride price, so Deioneus stole some of Ixion's horses in retaliation. Ixion concealed his resentment and invited his father-in-law to a feast at Larissa. When Deioneus arrived, Ixion pushed him into a bed of burning coals and wood.<br /> Ixion went mad, defiled by his act; the neighboring princes were so offended by this act of treachery and violation of xenia that they refused to perform the rituals that would cleanse Ixion of his guilt. Thereafter, Ixion lived as an outlaw and was shunned. By killing his father-in-law, Ixion was reckoned the first man guilty of kin-slaying in Greek mythology.<br /> This act alone would warrant Ixion a terrible punishment, but Zeus took pity on Ixion and brought him to Olympus and introduced him at the table of the gods. Instead of being grateful, Ixion grew lustful for Hera,<br /> Zeus found out about his intentions and made a cloud in the shape of Hera, which became known as Nephele (from nephos &quot;cloud&quot;) and tricked Ixion into coupling with it. From the union of Ixion and the false-Hera cloud came Imbros or Centauros, who mated with the Magnesian mares on Mount Pelion, engendering the race of Centaurs, who are called the Ixionidae from their descent.<br /> Ixion was expelled from Olympus and blasted with a thunderbolt. Zeus ordered Hermes to bind Ixion to a winged fiery wheel that was always spinning. Therefore, Ixion was bound to a burning solar wheel for all eternity, at first spinning across the heavens, but in later myth transferred to Tartarus<br /> <br /> <b>Proto-vampires aka. neanderthals of the vampiric race</b><br /> To be honest, this is the closest I got to invent my own based on the tale from the 1st ed Nosferatu Clan Book where the narrator describes the Cainites as &quot;cavemans&quot; basically and the canon &quot;fact&quot; Absimiliard hunted Saberthoot tigers as a vampire and before that<br /> And mixing the tale of the <b>Khara</b> the weresabertooths<br /> According to the oral traditions shared among the Bastet, the Khara first came forth when the human wizard, Palar and agreat sabre-tooth joined forces against a mighty manifestation of Asura (what Garou call the Wyrm) in the form of a great dragon. Although the two managed to slay the dragon, they were grievously wounded. Their mingled blood, alongside the tears of their Kin, touched Seline\u2019s heart and she descended from the Moon to the Earth to mourn alongside them. Her tears formed the first Khara, born from the blood and tears of cats, men, and the Moon. Mixed in their essence, however, was a shard of the dragon\u2019s essence and soon, the Khara grew proud and terrorized their Kinfolk like the Asura had done. Enraged, Seline cursed them with their weakness against silver, as well with the essential Curse of Rage. As Luna\u2019s behest, the first tribe was divided across the world and the Khara soon found mates in the native great cats. Their bloodline diluted further and further, until the nine tribes of the modern Bastet were born.<br /> The two tale could be used together since not only the Khara were tainted by the Asura<br /> The whole mess with Banes and other nasty things that plague Gaia comes from the Asura, a being that is the incarnated form of Cahlash's hate against his brother Rajah and his despair from his loneliness. When Cahlash ripped the Asura from himself, he hoped that the Asura would destroy the things of Rajah, but the Asura turned into a multitude of serpents that infested the world, leading to the creation of Banes, fomori, vampires, and other rotten things.<br /> These things could be interpreted, proto-vampires in the stone age existed before Caine and Absimiliard, the &quot;civilized&quot; vampiric race of cainites.<br /> And like how the Homo Sapiens drove the neanderthals to extinction, the spawns of Caine destroyed the Asura-vampires<br /> <br /> Honorary mention goes to the <b>Drowned Legacies</b><br /> They had to come somewhere too... (sure could be Cainites)<br /> The Samedi are hinted is actually not a Cappadocian offshot, but the Baron is the real thing, a Haitian Death God that inhabit a corpse and spread his &quot;Gifts&quot;. In that regard, Baron Samedi could be like Set, a God in Mortal form with his own brood and race of Vampire\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> These are my Vampire-races, and always had a tons of fun, using them\u200b <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T12:58:50-07:00","id":1510238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510230#post1510230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And like how the Homo Sapiens drove the neanderthals to extinction, the spawns of Caine destroyed the Asura-vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still up in the air IRL what ultimately caused<i> Homo sapiens neanderthalis</i> to die off. In the WoD, however, there was an answer given in various W20 books, most notably Shattered Dreams - the Ananasi ritually murdered most of them, and the loss was non-recoverable. As a result, shifters migrated over to <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>.<br /> <br /> (IRL, there is also some evidence that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rnqT0K5Ls2I\" target=\"_blank\">this time marked a single amino acid mutation in a transketolase-like enzyme</a> that caused neural precursor cells to grow in far, far greater number than they would otherwise. This coincides with a tool revolution in the fossil record.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:09:07-07:00","id":1510243,"title":"","content":"I hew closely to a generic version of the official VtM myth. There was an antedeluvian world. There is a single progenitor of vampires who had several childer and they in turn had thirteen others. That antedeluvian world was destroyed in some kind of deluge or cataclysm. Thirteen vampires survived to found the clans we now know. Whether or not the 13 Antedeluvians were technically vampires in the sense we know them today before the Deluge, or were something else and their vampire nature was a result of the changes in the world after that catastrophe is up for debate. The antedeluvian world operated under different principles than this one, and the Severing (the rise of the Gauntlet and the division between the spirit world and physical world) happened at that time.<br /> <br /> That is usually the most detail I use because I don't feel it's necessary to do anything more to run a chronicle, and I don't want to step on player speculation.<br /> <br /> However, I do have some ideas. The antedeluvian world was not Stone Age humanity. And it was not the typical Biblical view. It was more like Atlantis / Hyborian Age / Hellboy's Hyperborea. It's not incompatible with the Biblical view, but acknowledges the Biblical view is massively incomplete since whatever knowledge survived the catastrophe just could not be properly understood by Neolithic or Bronze Age humanity. Other Deluge myths, occult traditions of a world before this one, the pseudo-archaeology of Graham Hancock and others, and the psychic theories of people like Helena Blavatsky, Edgar Cayce, and many others all play a role and contain some evidence as well of what that antedeluvian world was like. I am a huge fan of how Mike Mignola and John Arcudi have blended in Biblical lore, cosmic horror, Sword &amp; Sorcery, the conventions of gothic horror, folklore, and many other things in their portrayal of the Hellboy setting. That's exactly where I want to slot my World of Darkness. Exactly how the progenitor became a vampire is up to debate, but is definitely a result of some spirit that gave rise to later myths of Lilith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:28:24-07:00","id":1510249,"title":"","content":"I enjoy coming up with these. I'll probably never use any (or at least more than presenting them as some kind of newborn theory or fringe cult), because I don't like characters knowing The Truth\u2122. Maybe if I ever do a game centred on Gehenna or Golconda it'll come up.<br /> <br /> 1) The first was Abel, not Caine 2) The first was actually Seth, whose true story has been confused with and falsely attributed to the 3rd generation vampire Sutekh<br /> 3) Humans kind of originally derive from the first generations of vampires - the Antediluvian race - not the other way around. (generations 2-16 are human-vampire hybrids and life for humanity in Antediluvian times <i>sucked</i>)<br /> 4) The first generation, who were multitude, were prehistoric people who committed acts of great violence, defilement or negative emotion that drew the attention of Unpleasant Things and resulted in their transformation.<br /> 5) The first vampires were cosmic horrors (Neverborn? Malfeans? Formorians? Abyssal entities? Maybe something worse), the subsequent generations are their essence/offspring living in human bodies. Although the further it spreads through the mundane world, the further it dilutes.<br /> 6) The Primordians got it right. Vampires are composed of fragments of the Triat cut off from the source and trapped together in the same host, driving each other and themselves insane in eternal torment and their hunger is an attempt to reconnect by syphoning off of the rest of the world. (Weaver dominates, Wyrm is the second biggest influence as the Beast, and the Wyld is the remaining sparks of dynamism lingering behind them)<br /> <br /> And one of my personal off the wall favourites:<br /> 7)<br /> The first vampire (which may not even have been a sentient being) was the thing that inspired the legends of the philosopher's stone; vitae is the elixir of life and undeath is actually the second stage (albedo/purification) of the magnum opus.<br /> <br /> Nigredo/Decay: The Embrace -&gt; Albedo/Purification: Undeath -&gt; Citrinitas/Enlightenment: Golconda -&gt; Rubedo/Completion: Perfect immortal being with 10 in every discipline and zero weaknesses or drawbacks <br /> <br /> (Basically, split the original human into the human psyche and the vampiric beast, reconcile them in the suspire, entering golconda and freeing yourself of the drawbacks of the curse, then focus on perfecting yourself now that generational limits are no longer in your way. Generation is a thing because the imperfect and incomplete elixir dilutes with every embrace)<br /> <br /> Oh, and the creation of the original philosopher's stone may or may not have involved Fullmetal Alchemist genocide tier human sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure I'll come up with more bizzare ideas as time goes on.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T02:00:36-07:00","id":1510338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires#post1510211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I personally love notion of Set being the father of the undead and selecting 12 people to fight his enemies. I\u2019m curious if you came up with your backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently entertained the concept and the idea that there are some ancient vampiric and undead persons who are wholly unrelated to the forebears and founders we know. Mostly they at the very least know each other socially or through some cooperation and maintained antagonisms, but there are some - like Mekhet, Set or Sutekh, or the 2nd Generation ( Zillah, Irad, Enoch ) who are distinctly separate.<br /> <br /> They might have all sort of different and interesting powers, unique bloodlines, guilds, or groups established centuries ago, and also they might display and stand for their own particular attitudes and methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T07:37:55-07:00","id":1510356,"title":"","content":"I've got several rough outlines. Pretty much all of them are based on Judeo-Christian mythology or pseudu-Judeo-Christian mythology but you know, that works for me in regards to Vampire.<br /> <br /> The two which I find to be the best are the following:<br /> <br /> 1. The Antediluvians are Nephilim who survived the Flood by turning themselves undead as the waters rose.<br /> <br /> 2. The Antediluvians are children of Lilth with various lovers; Brujah from Caine, Set from the Serpent in the Garden and so on. The reason they are undead is because of the curse that Lilith's children should die, so she turned them undead to get around the curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:20:50-07:00","id":1510370,"title":"","content":"I like option 2 a fair bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:35:23-07:00","id":1510372,"title":"","content":"I had a creation myth in a roman game that each of the clan founders was born from the shadow of the olympians when Pandoras box was opened<br /> <br /> Zues-ventrue<br /> Posidon-lasombra<br /> Athena-brujah<br /> <br /> And so on, some of the founders where mysteries to hide the gods shame and apollo specifically didn't have one due to being a sun god. The idea was they manifested the gods shortcomings and sins as dark reflections in the last 13 members of the silver race.<br /> <br /> the other idea was in neoplatonic philosophy thought they existed as a reflection of man inverted as nous. The soul has left the body for the higher Realm with the beast replacing it. Golconda being a state where the nous soul achieved a state closer to the One","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-01-2023, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T09:59:39-07:00","id":1510373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510372#post1510372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a creation myth in a roman game that each of the clan founders was born from the shadow of the olympians when Pandoras box was opened<br /> <br /> Zues-ventrue<br /> Posidon-lasombra<br /> Athena-brujah<br /> <br /> And so on, some of the founders where mysteries to hide the gods shame and apollo specifically didn't have one due to being a sun god. The idea was they manifested the gods shortcomings and sins as dark reflections in the last 13 members of the silver race.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you write who from the Founders you paired up with who from the Greek ( or Roman ) patrons and deities ? Are there assignments that are distinctly interesting and curious under some considerations and criteria ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:01:10-07:00","id":1510378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510373#post1510373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you write who from the Founders you paired up with who from the Greek ( or Roman ) patrons and deities ? Are there assignments that are distinctly interesting and curious under some considerations and criteria ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aphroditie-nosferatu/toreador (bitterly contested)<br /> bachus/heceta-malkav (contested)<br /> artemis-gangrel<br /> hephastus- toreador/nosferatu<br /> saulot-maintains the myth of Caine<br /> Set-set Maintains their own faith.<br /> ????-tzmisce, speculated to be Kronos or gaia.<br /> Hermes-ravnos<br /> ????-haqim<br /> <br /> this outlook is still found in carmarilla elders and has gained traction in the anarchs but is considered heresy in the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-01-2023, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:33:51-07:00","id":1510384,"title":"","content":"My ST already asked if he could remake an origin story based on Eldritch creatures, but it didn't go ahead, I'm doing something like that myself for the whole WoD, I'll post when it's ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:12:43-07:00","id":1510408,"title":"","content":"Maybe Ares/Mars or Phobias for Haqim as both could fit for founders of the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:48:13-07:00","id":1510414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510408#post1510408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Ares/Mars or Phobias for Haqim as both could fit for founders of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, the issue was the assamites (and the tzmisce) were a foreign clan and the roman kindred considered them at least three clans due to the castes. Conversly the assamites, strongly aligned with the partian empire (and had a large number of clans present in their territory) ascribed to a form of zorostrianism so didn't really think much of the idea. The Roman kindred would be very reluctant to associate Mars with an enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T16:29:41-07:00","id":1510436,"title":"","content":"I remember there being a thread here (forgot the title and OP) giving us an alternate in-universe origin myth based on Greek mythology; nine Clans descended from the nine children of Orpheus, born in the Underworld and of the third generation counting from Olympus. Drinking blood was staving off the \u2018pull\u2019 of Hades, who still considers them under his rule. Burning in sunlight was the wrath of Apollo, the clan founders\u2019 grandfather and technically the first generation of all Kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my idea, I once toyed with the idea of vampires being descended from the Urge Wyrm of Greed. Felt more \u2018natural\u2019 than the Bloody Man story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-01-2023, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T12:35:19-07:00","id":1510513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510414#post1510414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly, the issue was the assamites (and the tzmisce) were a foreign clan and the roman kindred considered them at least three clans due to the castes. Conversly the assamites, strongly aligned with the partian empire (and had a large number of clans present in their territory) ascribed to a form of zorostrianism so didn't really think much of the idea. The Roman kindred would be very reluctant to associate Mars with an enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could rationalize as finding the equalivant god for that culture. I also think that maybe Phobias would be a good progenitor for the Baali for the fear aspect that this bloodline is known for and it might work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T18:43:37-07:00","id":1510540,"title":"","content":"My default for my Vampire games over the past decade or so has been that there are/were the 13 clan founders, but before that? No one knows. The idea of a first vampire isn't uncommon, but the idea of it being the Biblical Cain (no extra e) is relatively new. There really isn't any sort of &quot;second generation&quot; between those two steps though. (This is mostly just because I prefer the idea that, if there was a first vampire, he chose these 13 weirdos for the embrace for a reason, and is one some level inherently responsible for whatever shenanigans they and their offspring have gotten up to over the millennium.) <br /> <br /> In the Dark Ages, I have the commonly preached belief that the clan founders were all fallen angels, with the seven High Clan ones (Brujah, Cappadocian, Lasombra, Salubri, Toreador, Tzimisce, Ventrue) fell for &quot;noble&quot; reasons, while the six Low Clan founders fell for more base reasons. This then justifies the High and Low clan split. And yes, it's a very self-serving story for the benefit of those in power. <br /> <br /> My head canon is that India's Hindu vampires believe that their founders are/were the Rakshasa, created by the breath of Brahma at the end of the Age of Truth only to be instantly consumed with by an insatiable bloodthirst and attempted to devour their creator. For this crime, Vishnu banished them to earth. By the age of the Ramayana and Mahabharata, there are many Rakshasa, but the two most influential are Ravana, who is bloodthirsty and wicked, and Vibhishana, who is noble and righteous. The followers of the former are akin to Europe's Sabbat, while the latter are the majority and more akin to the Camarilla's mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T20:10:47-07:00","id":1510549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510356#post1510356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Antediluvians are Nephilim who survived the Flood by turning themselves undead as the waters rose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have played with this idea too. It's why I said the Antedeluvians (and hence their antecedents) may not have technically been vampires before the Deluge. They may or may not have intentionally turned themselves undead, as it might also be an inadvertent result of something they did earlier (or someone else like &quot;Lilith&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T06:36:36-07:00","id":1510587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510540#post1510540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Dark Ages, I have the commonly preached belief that the clan founders were all fallen angels, with the seven High Clan ones (Brujah, Cappadocian, Lasombra, Salubri, Toreador, Tzimisce, Ventrue) fell for &quot;noble&quot; reasons, while the six Low Clan founders fell for more base reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any more divisions and categories other than Low ( or Common or Normal ) and High ( or Aristocratic or Elite ) ? Is there perhaps at least one extra, curious, mysterious, and different category ?<br /> <br /> I am an enthusiastic, positive, and optimistic supporter of novel, suprising, and radical factions, groups, and categories. For example the Dwarf faction in Heroes of Might and Magic 5 and 7, the Atlantean faction in Age of Mythology, or the various Roman and Italian nations in games like Europa Universalis Four and Medieval Total War Two. Hence I was wondering if an additional group could exist within the distinctions you described. A team or a group with it's own particular themes, qualities, goals, methods, and capabilities.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T09:59:01-07:00","id":1510803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510549#post1510549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have played with this idea too. It's why I said the Antedeluvians (and hence their antecedents) may not have technically been vampires before the Deluge. They may or may not have intentionally turned themselves undead, as it might also be an inadvertent result of something they did earlier (or someone else like &quot;Lilith&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>True that.<br /> <br /> One reason that I also based the idea on the Nephilim is that it would allow Cainites to interact with creatures who are not Cainites but connected to them according to this myth. I am here thinking of the Grigori angels who sired the Nephilim, the mortal women, taught all manner of sorceries by the Grigori angels, who gave birth to the Nephilim as well as the spirits of the Nephilim who died in the Flood. Lots of cool stuff there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T09:08:45-07:00","id":1510885,"title":"","content":"Writer Mick Farren or was it Farris used the Nephilim lore for his take on the vampire myths. But it was more science fiction based origins for there species then a supernatural one and I still found it a good source material for depicting elders and ancients whom humanity has withered over the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-06-2023, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:32:15-07:00","id":1510936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510587#post1510587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there any more divisions and categories other than Low ( or Common or Normal ) and High ( or Aristocratic or Elite ) ? Is there perhaps at least one extra, curious, mysterious, and different category ?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere default to being viewed as one of the Low Clans because they're upstarts of questionable lineage. But I suspect most of the Dark Ages bloodlines are viewed as &quot;something other&quot;, similar to the way certain mortal groups don't really fit neatly into the Nobility/Clergy/Commoner division. <br /> <br /> As far as alternate vampire origins from fiction go, I did enjoy the one from The Strain, in which an angel was torn apart, with the legs, arms, and head/torso all becoming the original vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T00:05:07-07:00","id":1510961,"title":"","content":"in my head Canon/ house rules the truth is there was no cain no second generation, it all started with the 13 clan founders. thousands of years ago a great spirit wind ripped through the underworld, so devastating that all the ghosts of the ancient world where washed away only the strongest spirits had any hope of survival, in a desperate attempt to shield themselves from harm the 13 death lords of the underworld hurled there essence into the lands of the living seeking refuge in the bodies of the recently dead, binding themselves to unliving flesh. in time each discovered that to maintain these bodies they needed new infusions of life, gathered most easily from the blood of the living.<br /> <br /> they found in time that they could taint the souls of the living creating other half living beings that feed on living essence and over time the clans are born, but also over time the conciousness of the death lords was drawn back into the underworld causing there physical forms to slumber for long years. This is also why those like Giovanni and tremere who have devoured the clan founders seemed to shortly after suffer from it, they didn't just absorb there power, they took the spirit of God of death into there own body.<br /> <br /> I also like to think that the first hosts where all recently dead mages and that Lilith was a winter court true fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T08:01:46-07:00","id":1511728,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside whether they're factual in-universe or not, the kindred of antiquity probably had half a dozen origins that reflected the human religion around them. (I also like to think that most clan names are recent, and the Nosferatu's most ancient name is the Tribe/Clan/Children/House of Abisimillard and the name Nosferatu came in in 1922, when some fledgling sewer rat made a Count Orlok reference and the name went memetic.)<br /> <br /> But anyway, during some research on Celtic mythology I came across somebody saying that there was folklore about souls in service to the Welsh god Arawn who returned to Earth in his retinue when the god rode out to hunt escaped souls and sinners. Their job was to drink the blood from the living and corpses. I know that as the old folklore got Christianized that Arawn became a king of hell and damned souls were doomed to his service, though I'm not sure the vampiric bit is genuine folklore. I'm definitely using it though. (Also Arawn was a shapeshifter and a sorcerer with a menagerie of spirits and weird animals, so this is also a great excuse to add more Tzimisce! And maybe some Cappadocians for the necromancy. Always a happy occasion.)<br /> <br /> Persia from 600 BCE onward would probably be drawing on Angra Mainyu/Ahriman and daevas and possibly some proto-Abyss Mysticism from the Lasombra. Apparently, when Ahriman created evil opposites to everything Ahura Mazda created, he couldn't manage to replicate humans, but maybe from the vampire perspective, he could either corrupt a human into a vampire or else created some kind of failed, lesser mockery of humanity - possibly a byproduct of his attack on Gayomard, the first human.<br /> (I would also expect intense theological debates between ancient Persian kindred about whether the struggle between inner light and dark and the promise of rebirth for the damned in the reborn world applies to them, or if as vampires and embodiments of <i>druj</i> they're literally made of falsehood and darkness and their notions of having humanity is just them lying to and corrupting themselves just as they were made to do the world around them.)<br /> <br /> As for Rome, I'd tend to lean on the Striges. Not exactly in the same way Requiem did, maybe, but still (although the fratricide angle of &quot;one demigod son of a war god kills the other one and then vampirism results&quot; carries over well). Blood-sucking monsters from hell is a good starting point for looking for vampire origins in antiquity.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Egypt was dominated by Setite theology, or if there were several theories pushing back? My eyes are starting to glaze over badly though, so something to think about some other time, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T12:54:57-07:00","id":1511734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avaron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510211-have-you-created-your-own-origins-for-the-vampires?p=1510961#post1510961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lilith was a winter court true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you try, and do you desire to expand and elaborate in regard to this theory or story about Mistress Lilith ? This idea seems unique and reasonable tto a meaningful extent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}